    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Hegarty Properties are delighted to present this detached home at Lahard, Whitegate. A private and beautifully maintained residence set on generous grounds of approximately 0.96 acres, just a short drive from the coast and from the vibrant town of Midleton. Built in 1974 and cared for with pride throughout, the property is complemented by a suite of renewable energy features that help keep running costs down.\r\nPerfectly positioned in the coastal townland of Lahard, the property enjoys countryside views and a setting that is second to none. Inch beach a sandy Green Coast strand and one of East Cork's best-loved surf spots is within walking distance, along with the cliff-top walk out to Power Head Lighthouse and the ever-popular Sweaty Sanctuary sea sauna down on the beach. \r\nThe surrounding villages offer a genuine, welcoming community. Whitegate and Aghada provide everyday amenities, with Corkbeg Coffee on Whitegate's pier serving specialty coffee and homemade treats beside panoramic views across Cork Harbour to Cobh, while the charming Poc ar Buile at nearby Ballinrostig is a traditional Irish pub famed for its roaring fires and lively trad music nights. A choice of primary schools is close at hand, making this an ideal setting for families.\r\nFor all its rural, seaside feel, the property is exceptionally well connected. The market town of Midleton with its supermarkets, restaurants, cafés is around 20 minutes' drive, while Cork city is approximately 35 minutes away. The Cork–Waterford N25 and Cork International Airport are both within easy reach for onward connections.\r\nFormerly home to Boarding Kennels, the property also offers genuine scope for a buyer seeking a rural home with room to work, keep animals or run a small enterprise (subject to the usual consents), with two existing dog kennels and almost an acre of grounds.\r\n\r\nAccommodation comprises: Entrance Porch, Open-Plan Sitting Room / Kitchen / Dining Area, Sunroom, 4 Bedrooms and Family Bathroom.\r\n(circa 112.42 m²)\r\nGuide Price: €395,000"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Porch: \t\tBright, tiled entrance porch.\t\r\n\r\nOpen-Plan Sitting Room\r\n/ Kitchen / Dining:\tA generous, light-filled open-plan living space warmed by electric underfloor heating. The fully fitted kitchen offers excellent storage and a tiled splashback, with induction hob, oven, dishwasher, fridge and freezer. Tiled flooring, with double doors leading through to the sunroom and garden.\r\n\r\nSunroom:\tRear-aspect sunroom with timber flooring and doors opening to the garden.\r\n\r\nMaster Bedroom:\tWell-proportioned double with timber flooring.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2: \t\tDouble bedroom with timber flooring.\r\n\t\t\t \t\r\nBedroom 3: \tSingle bedroom with timber flooring.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4: \tDouble bedroom with timber flooring.\r\n\r\nFamily Bathroom:\tFully tiled, with shower, W.C. and w.h.b.\r\n\r\nSale to include:\t All white goods, blinds, electric fittings and table in sunroom.\r\n \r\nOutside:\r\nTo the front, a boundary wall leads to a gravelled driveway providing ample off-street parking. The south-facing rear enjoys lawned gardens set on grounds of approximately 0.96 acres, with lovely countryside views, a garden shed, outdoor taps and two dog kennels.\r\n\r\nServices: \r\n•\tElectric underfloor heating to the main living area \r\n•\tInfrared (IR) heating panels throughout, powered by solar \r\n•\tSolar PV panels \r\n•\tWell water \r\n•\tSeptic tank drainage"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "•\tDetached home, built 1974 \r\n•\tRenewable energy: solar PV with infrared panels throughout and electric underfloor heating in the main living area \r\n•\tBright open-plan living, with a south-facing rear garden \r\n•\tGenerous grounds of approximately 0.96 acres (0.39 ha) with countryside views \r\n•\tAttic accessed via Stira\r\n•\tSuperb coastal location walking distance to Inch Beach\r\n•\tFreehold: Folio CK101551F"
      },
